      ],
      "optional_open": true,
      "deadline": null,
      "recipient_id": "june_arlen",
      "sender_id": "leonie",
      "envelope": {
        "recipient": "June Arlen",
        "address": "water-damaged",
        "back": "Detached forwarding label partly attached",
        "recovered_fields": {
          "original_address": "Rose Court 3C",
          "forwarding_recipient": "June Arlen",
          "forwarding_destination": "North Pier Hostel",
          "forwarding_valid_from": "2024-07-20",
          "forwarding_valid_until": "2025-07-19"
        }
      },
      "body": "June,\n\nI finally developed the photographs from the storm night. Half of them are just black water and one ridiculous picture of my thumb.\n\nThere is one good photograph of the lighthouse, though. I made two prints. Yours is in the envelope.\n\nYou were right about the clouds clearing after midnight. I hated that you were right, because I had already complained for three hours.\n\nSee you when I am back in town.\n\nLeonie",
      "body_source": "04_VERTICAL_SLICE/CASE_BIBLE_FINAL.md",
      "private": true,
      "clues": [
