    {
      "id": "case04",
      "title": "Six Summers Late",
      "type": "recovered_archive_item",
      "initial_envelope_state": "aged_intact",
      "legal_dispositions": [
        "deliver",
        "archive_review",
        "hold_for_verification"
      ],
      "optional_open": true,
      "deadline": null,
      "recipient_id": "june_arlen",
      "sender_id": "",
      "envelope": {
        "recipient": "June Arlen",
        "address": "Rose Court 3C",
        "date": "2020-07-20",
        "return": "",
        "archive_mark": "HV / HOLD"
      },
      "body": "June,\n\nI wrote an uglier version of this first. I tore it up because it made me sound certain, and I wasn’t.\n\nI was angry that you left the rehearsal. Then I was angrier that everyone kept asking me whether I was all right, as if you had done something to me instead of simply choosing something for yourself.\n\nThe honest part is this: I wanted you to stay. Not because the band needed you. Not because Solmere needed you. Because I did.\n\nI did not know how to say that without making it sound like a debt.\n\nIf you leave tomorrow, go. I will survive being angry. I would rather be angry than have you stay because you feel sorry for me.\n\nI just did not want the last true thing between us to be the stupid argument behind the community center.\n\nMira",
      "body_source": "04_VERTICAL_SLICE/CASE_BIBLE_FINAL.md",
      "private": true,
      "clues": [
        "case04_archive_mark",
        "old_music_photo",
